        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">12 &mdash; FAQ</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        {[
          { q: "What is branded content?", a: "Branded content is any content that a brand funds where the primary purpose is to inform, entertain, or inspire the audience rather than directly sell a product. The brand is the sponsor, not the subject. It includes editorial articles, video series, social creator content, podcasts, and interactive experiences. The content earns attention on its own merits while building positive brand associations over time." },
          { q: "How is branded content different from advertising?", a: "Traditional advertising interrupts the audience to deliver a product message. Branded content is the content itself — it delivers value (information, entertainment, inspiration) that the audience seeks out willingly. Advertising says 'buy this product.' Branded content says 'here is something useful or interesting, brought to you by this brand.' The audience relationship is fundamentally different because branded content earns attention rather than buying interruptions." },
          { q: "What types of branded content work best in 2026?", a: "Short-form video (TikTok, Reels, Shorts) delivers the widest reach and fastest feedback loops. Creator-led social content combines authenticity with distribution. Long-form content (documentaries, podcast series, in-depth guides) builds deeper brand associations. Interactive content (quizzes, calculators, tools) generates the highest engagement and first-party data capture. The best strategies combine short-form for awareness with long-form for depth." },
          { q: "How much does branded content cost?", a: "Costs vary widely by format. Short-form social video with micro-creators: $200-$3,000 per piece. Editorial articles: $2,000-$25,000 per piece. Podcast episodes: $5,000-$50,000 per episode. Long-form documentary video: $10,000-$250,000+. Interactive tools: $10,000-$100,000+. These are production costs only — add 30-100% for paid distribution and amplification. OKAD provides all-in pricing with production and distribution bundled. Contact olga@okad.agency for a custom quote." },
          { q: "How do I measure branded content ROI?", a: "Use a three-layer measurement framework. Engagement metrics (views, watch time, shares, saves) show whether the audience consumed the content. Brand metrics (aided recall, consideration lift, sentiment) show whether perceptions changed. Business metrics (traffic, leads, pipeline, revenue) show bottom-line impact. Brand lift studies and incrementality tests provide the most rigorous measurement. Track all three layers to capture the full value of branded content." },
          { q: "How long before branded content shows results?", a: "Expect initial engagement data within 1-2 weeks of publishing. Meaningful brand lift data requires 4-8 weeks of consistent content and sufficient sample sizes for lift studies. Compounding returns — where your content library, audience relationships, and distribution efficiency all reinforce each other — typically emerge after 3-6 months of sustained output. Branded content is a long-term investment, not a quick-hit tactic." },
          { q: "Should I create branded content in-house or work with an agency?", a: "In-house works well if you have existing content production capabilities, creator relationships, and platform expertise. An agency like OKAD makes sense if you want to launch quickly without building an internal team, need access to a network of vetted creators, or want to scale content volume beyond what your team can handle. Many brands use a hybrid model: in-house for brand-owned content (blog, email, social posts) and agency for creator-powered branded content." },
          { q: "How do I choose the right creators for branded content?", a: "Prioritize niche fit over follower count. A creator with 15K followers in your exact niche will produce more effective branded content than a creator with 500K followers in a tangential space. Evaluate content quality (hooks, pacing, production), audience demographics (age, gender, geography match your target), engagement rate (active audience, not just followers), and reliability (meeting deadlines, following briefs, professional communication)." },
          { q: "Can branded content be used as paid ads?", a: "Yes, and it should be. Branded content that performs well organically can be amplified as paid ads using TikTok Spark Ads, Meta Partnership Ads, or whitelabel promotion. This is one of the most effective ad strategies available because the content has already proven it resonates with a real audience. See our guide on branded content ads for the complete breakdown of delivery methods and platform mechanics." },
          { q: "What platforms should I prioritize for branded content?", a: "Start where your audience spends the most time. For Gen Z and millennials: TikTok and Instagram. For professionals and B2B: LinkedIn and YouTube. For niche communities: YouTube and podcasts. For broad consumer reach: TikTok, Instagram, and YouTube. Master one platform before expanding to others. Cross-posting identical content rarely works — each platform has different audience expectations and format norms." },
          { q: "How does branded content fit with other marketing channels?", a: "Branded content works best as a mid-funnel complement to upper-funnel awareness ads and lower-funnel performance marketing. Use branded content to build trust and consideration, then retarget engaged viewers with direct response ads. Branded content also feeds content marketing (repurpose for blog, email, social), PR (newsworthy branded content earns media coverage), and sales enablement (share branded content with prospects during the sales process)." },
          { q: "Can OKAD produce branded content for my brand?", a: "Yes. OKAD provides end-to-end branded content services: strategy development, creator casting from our network of 600+ vetted creators, brief development, content production, paid amplification across TikTok, Instagram, YouTube, and LinkedIn, and monthly performance reporting. We work with brands across e-commerce, SaaS, fintech, health and wellness, and consumer products. Email olga@okad.agency with your brand, product, and goals to get started." },
